      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-11T22:51:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can save about 100 bytes by changing the PD debug level from 2 to 1:\n\n```\n#define CONFIG_USB_PD_DEBUG_LEVEL 1\n```\n\nThat retains the PD logging of state transitions, but doesn\u0027t print out the raw PD packets.  However, it hardly seems worth the effort.\n\nSetting CONFIG_USB_PD_DEBUG_LEVEL to 0, will save considerable space. We won\u0027t be completely blind for debugging PD, as the PE state transitions are still logged - but without the state names.",
      "parentUuid": "05827a67_7475df21",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 164,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 164,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "44801308b6173567d0764970b2ca8cd2013219f1",
